# Copy to .env (gitignored). Everything has a working default.
#
# THIS FILE IS READ ON RANK 0 ONLY. Both ranks are launched from up.sh on this
# node, so there is no second .env to keep in step - that is the point, and it
# is the one place this recipe deliberately differs from the upstream one it
# was ported from (docs/decisions.md#glm53-flash).

# HF_TOKEN=hf_...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE MEMORY KNOB, and the failure that looks like something else
#
# 0.87 of 121 GiB needs ~106 GiB free AFTER vLLM's own ~9 GiB of init. A
# resident desktop session, a dashboard or a TTS service can put you under it
# by well below a GiB - the startup memory check then refuses, which reads as
# "the model does not fit" rather than "something else is holding a gigabyte".
# gx10-top will tell you which it is.
#
# The documented fallback, which fits with margin:
# GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.86
# MAX_MODEL_LEN=800000
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# DO NOT drop MAX_MODEL_LEN to 256000 to "free" KV. It is the first thing
# people try and it does the opposite: the logged pool is roughly concurrency x
# this cap, and the hybrid floor underneath it - mamba state plus the drafter's
# sliding window - barely moves with length. A smaller cap shrinks the pool.
# MAX_MODEL_LEN=1000000
# MAX_NUM_SEQS=4

# 2048, and the two halves of that number come from different places. The
# CEILING is hardware: 8192-token chunks oversubscribe the GB10 indexer top-k's
# shared memory and crash a long prefill around 300k tokens. The VALUE under it
# is measured - the published ladder has 2048 beating 1024 by +16% on an 8k
# cold prefill, and 3584 and 4096 both LOSING despite 3584 being page-aligned.
# `ws up vllm-prefill-ladder --chunk-tokens 2048` re-takes that table here.
# Never 8192, whatever a throughput argument says.
# MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=2048

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPECULATIVE DECODING
#
# dflash (default) - DFlash2 k=7, a separate ~2.3 GiB drafter.
# mtp              - the checkpoint's own head. No second download, ~2.5x
#                    slower on the source kit's structured bench.
# none             - measure the difference.
# SPEC_METHOD=dflash
# DRAFT_TOKENS=7
# MTP_TOKENS=2
#
# DRAFT_TP=2 shards the ~2.3 GiB drafter across both ranks. That is a MEMORY
# decision: vLLM sizes one KV pool for the whole server, so a drafter parked
# entirely on rank 0 costs its full 2.3 GiB out of a ~19 GiB budget on BOTH
# nodes. Sharding hands ~1.15 GiB back. The cost is that a draft step crosses
# the cable; measured upstream as no regression rather than as a win.
# DRAFT_TP=1
#
# NEVER put "attention_backend":"TRITON_ATTN" in SPEC_CONFIG. It is copied from
# an SM120 recipe and on this image that mask is causal INSIDE the draft block,
# which leaves draft position 0 healthy and collapses the rest. Measured on the
# source kit: structured decode fell from ~62 to ~29 tok/s and acceptance from
# 0.92 to 0.31, with the server reporting nothing wrong.
# SPEC_CONFIG={"method":"dflash","model":"incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2","num_speculative_tokens":7,"kv_cache_dtype":"auto","draft_sample_method":"probabilistic","rejection_sample_method":"standard","draft_tensor_parallel_size":2}
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Weights. The mirror is byte-identical to brandonmusic/GLM-5.3-Flash-tr3-4bpw
# snapshot 5ab363a8; it exists so this recipe stays fetchable if the upstream
# Hub id moves. The revision is pinned for the same reason a lockfile is - clear
# it to follow the branch.
# MODEL=Mia-AiLab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-TR3-4bpw
# MODEL_REVISION=25a44fdbf16862a46b7cc9921142c6c81350af2f
# DRAFT_MODEL=incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2

# Pin the image by digest if you want the guarantee in writing. Both ranks pull
# the same string either way, which is the property that stops the silent
# mismatched-rank hang.
# IMAGE=ghcr.io/miaai-lab/glm-5.3-flash-2x-dgx-sparks:exl3

# Vision is on. SKIP_MM_PROFILING is not optional with it - the max-size
# multimodal dummy profile OOMs this pool at init. Language-only if you want
# the memory back:
# LANGUAGE_MODEL_ONLY=1
# LIMIT_MM={"image":4,"video":1}

# Rendezvous. Auto-detected from the default route.
# MASTER_ADDR=192.168.1.70
# PEER=poseidon

# Leave IB_HCA and IB_GID_INDEX unset unless a log shows the wrong device or
# `ibv_modify_qp` errno 61 on the worker rank about a minute into the launch.
# The upstream recipe pins NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=3 and then has to validate it,
# because 3 is all-zero on one card of some pairs; this repo asks NCCL to pick
# the RoCEv2 IPv4 GID instead. `gx10-interconnect` prints the table.
# IB_HCA=rocep1s0f0,roceP2p1s0f0
# IB_GID_INDEX=2

# JIT caches survive `docker rm` here. Losing them re-JITs mid-collective on
# TP=2 and trips NCCL's 600 s watchdog, which reports a hang, not a compile.
# JIT_CACHE=/home/you/.cache/vllm-glm53-exl3

# 8893, so it does not collide with the other serving workspaces.
# PORT=8893

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL BEARER AUTH. vLLM reads VLLM_API_KEY natively as the fallback for
# `--api-key`, so setting it here keeps the key out of argv - out of `ps`, out
# of the container command line, and out of the `non-default args` line vLLM
# logs at every boot. The bench workspaces read the same value from API_KEY.
# Empty means unauthenticated, which is the default everywhere in this repo.
# VLLM_API_KEY=

# vLLM subtracts a PREDICTED CUDA-graph footprint from the KV pool before
# capturing. 0 hands back whatever the prediction overshot, with graphs still
# on. Untried here, and this is the workspace with the least room to absorb an
# under-estimate - reach for it when the pool is what is binding, not by default.
# CG_ESTIMATE=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JIT SHAPE WARMUP. ./warmup.sh waits for /health and then burns the DFlash2
# BLOCK ladder, the three sampler variants and the batch shapes, so the first
# real client is not the first JIT on TP=2 - where a compile inside a
# collective leaves the other rank waiting. It is not run automatically: the
# cost of skipping it is latency on a handful of early requests, never
# correctness, and nothing here has measured that it matters on this cluster.
# WARMUP_HEALTH_WAIT=1800
# WARMUP_REQ_TIMEOUT=240
